1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,430
I love parades.

2
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:06,420
The Thanksgiving Day parade is always such great fun.

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:09,670
Look at that Superman balloon!

4
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:16,120
Wowee! Just floating along high above Central Park West.

5
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Don't you just love it?

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,250
Oh, and the bands and the music.

7
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:22,530
John Philip Sousa.

8
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:24,270
I love his music.

9
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:31,550
Da dada da da dada da da da da da da dada.

10
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:35,660
Oh, look at that float, Robbie.

11
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:38,090
Look at those funny-looking clowns.

12
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:40,410
It's for kids.

13
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:44,380
Maybe so, but parades always make me feel like a kid.

14
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:47,690
Remember when you and your dad and I

15
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:51,530
went to the Thanksgiving Day parade?

16
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:59,410
You were four or five years old, I think.

17
00:00:59,410 --> 00:01:03,180
Hello, hello.... Oh, hi, Susan.

18
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:09,210
How are you?... Here's Mom.

19
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:11,260
Hello, Susan.

20
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:14,980
Yes, he missed a phone call from Alexandra.

21
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:17,460
Yes, I know, but he'll get over it.

22
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:20,230
Good. Then you'll be here about five?

23
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:21,650
Oh, fine.

24
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:25,630
I look forward to seeing you and Harry and Michelle.

25
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:27,320
Drive carefully.

26
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,470
Good-bye.

27
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:30,570
Taste Ellen's turkey dressing.

28
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:33,090
It's delicious.

29
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:34,380
I'm not surprised.

30
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:36,020
It's Grandma's recipe.

31
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:37,740
It's my favorite part of the meal.

32
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:40,210
What about my famous apple pie?

33
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:44,310
Dad, your apple pie is my favorite dessert.

34
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:45,450
How's the parade?

35
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:56,420
OK.

36
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,770
Mom! Is it for me?

37
00:01:58,770 --> 00:02:00,190
No, Robbie.

38
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:02,460
Who was it?

39
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,110
Wrong number.

40
00:02:04,110 --> 00:02:06,350
Philip, would you join me in the kitchen, please?

41
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:07,050
It's getting late.

42
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:08,870
We have vegetables to prepare.

43
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:09,830
Can I help with anything?

44
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:10,400
No, honey.

45
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,800
You just relax with Grandpa.

46
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,420
I'll get you to help serve later.

47
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:18,290
Ellen reminds me so much of Grandma.

48
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:20,310
What time does the Michigan football game come on?

49
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:20,990
Four.

50
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:22,930
Philip!

51
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:26,800
I'll be back to see the game.

52
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:30,850
Grandpa, when did Dad graduate from Michigan?

53
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:32,620
Let me think.

54
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:36,270
He graduated from medical school in 1960

55
00:02:36,270 --> 00:02:41,090
and from the University of Michigan in 1956.

56
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:42,460
Did you go to Michigan, too, Grandpa?

57
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:46,850
Yup. I graduated in 1937.

58
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:49,850
I've got to start thinking about college soon.
